cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Mouseion: a self-hosted reading environment for foreign-language learning"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hayes
    given-names: Justin
repository-code: "https://github.com/justin-hayes/mouseion"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23268985
abstract: >-
  Mouseion analyzes the ebooks in a learner's own library with Stanza, persists
  a normalized, dependency-parsed corpus, measures the learner's vocabulary
  coverage of each book, and prepares Anki recognition cards for the recurring
  unknown lemmas, using example sentences from the book itself. It supports
  German, Italian, and Modern Greek, with language-specific lemmatization
  (German separable verbs, pre-1996 orthography, Greek contractions), EPUB
  main-text selection, GDEX-informed example-sentence scoring, and a
  Wiktionary-derived dictionary index with recorded provenance.
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - natural language processing
  - corpus linguistics
  - lemmatization
  - concordance
  - second language acquisition
  - vocabulary
  - German
  - Italian
  - Modern Greek
